WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.080
This video says what SWATrust is and what
the four views of its page do.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.590
SWATrust is a port of SWAT+ to the Rust
language,

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.170
with a launcher that runs in your browser.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.595
SWAT+ is the Soil and Water Assessment
Tool Plus,

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:17.030
a watershed model written in Fortran.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.583
SWATrust reads the input files of a SWAT+
model,

00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:26.380
the files of its TxtInOut folder, and writes
output tables in the formats of SWAT+.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.640
SWATrust has two programs.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.680
The engine simulates a model.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.353
The launcher is a page in the web browser
of your computer,

00:00:34.353 --> 00:00:38.590
on which you choose models, run them, look
at the results and calibrate.

00:00:39.091 --> 00:00:41.521
The left column of the page names four
views.

00:00:42.023 --> 00:00:46.643
In Set-up, you choose the models, the
years of the run and the output tables.

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.269
In Run, you start a run, watch it and stop
it.

00:00:59.741 --> 00:01:03.440
In Results, you look at the flow and the
water balance of a run,

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.001
and open its output folder.

00:01:08.551 --> 00:01:13.851
In Calibration, you calibrate a model on
measured flow and analyze its uncertainty.

00:01:14.351 --> 00:01:21.991
Quick start downloads one basin, 02070002,
North Branch Potomac, and runs it.
